  "interpretation": "The replacement outcomes differ only in an unobservable Quick Claw bit and have one quotient continuation. Postreplacement solvers recognize a two-sided-heal root. Fixed strategies retain every future opponent response. Reply probes change refinement order only: the complete root matrix remains intact, and a favorable selected reply never becomes a whole-game guarantee. Only fixed side-zero lower bounds enter unrestricted cells. These are full-information first-decision bounds with optimal continuation; no human calibration, deployed-policy improvement or global optimality is established."
